Falsifies `xtask::swish_check::boot::resolver_refusal_failure`, at the second boot's
`jig install uptime`, the one line that resolves a name at the prompt.

Architecture: x86_64
Line: jig install uptime

Milestone 892 (a std program at the prompt holds the network and a name resolver). The defect is
the progenitor placing `domain_name_resolver`'s budget `SPEND_ONLY`. Since milestone 824 (a retype
mints no right its budget lacks) the resolver's socket page then carries no `GRANT`, its
`SEND_CAP` to each socket it opens is refused, and every resolve answers "the resolver had no
socket page". `jig` falls back to the address the sources give, so every other line passes.

By hand:

    git apply xtask/falsifications/swish_check.boot.resolver_refusal_failure.patch
    script/swish-check --arch x86_64        # must exit non-zero, failing `jig install uptime`
    git apply -R xtask/falsifications/swish_check.boot.resolver_refusal_failure.patch

Expected to fail: `jig install uptime` prints `passed over
https://packages.basalt.test:8443/rolling/targets/uptime-0.1.0-x86_64.nifepkg: NetworkUnreachable
(the resolver had no socket page)`. Replayed 2026-10-18 (UTC): exit 1 naming that line; the fixed
tree prints `NotFound` there and exits 0.

